T1243	Quotation 203221 203271	"Excuse me, there's no one called Toskunov. . . ."
T1244	Quotation 203333 203352	"You needn't look,"
T1245	Entity 203378 203382	them
T1246	Entity 203353 203364	the old man
T1247	Cue 203365 203377	called after
T1248	Quotation 203384 203426	"I tell you there isn't, and there isn't."
T1249	Quotation 203427 203444	"Listen, auntie,"
T1250	Cue 203445 203449	said
T1251	Entity 203450 203463	Ivan Ivanitch
T1252	Quotation 203559 203605	"where is Nastasya Petrovna Toskunov's house?"
T1253	Entity 203476 203488	an old woman
T1254	Quotation 203661 203712	"Why, Nastasya Petrovna live in her own house now!"
T1255	Entity 203713 203716	she
T1256	Cue 203717 203722	cried
T1257	Quotation 203724 203858	"Lord! it is eight years since she married her daughter and gave up the house to her son-in-law! It's her son-in-law lives there now."
T1258	Quotation 203948 203978	"And where does she live now?"
T1259	Entity 203979 203992	Ivan Ivanitch
T1260	Cue 203993 203998	asked
T1261	Quotation 204000 204011	"Oh, Lord!"
T1262	Cue 204012 204017	cried
T1263	Entity 204018 204031	the old woman
T1264	Quotation 204068 204175	"She moved ever so long ago! It's eight years since she gave up her house to her son-in-law! Upon my word!"
T1265	Entity 204274 204287	Ivan Ivanitch
T1266	Cue 204288 204293	asked
T1270	Quotation 204307 204333	"Where does she live now?"
T1271	Entity 204334 204347	The old woman
T1272	Cue 204413 204420	shouted
T1273	Quotation 204449 204652	"Go straight on, straight on, straight on. You will pass a little red house, then you will see a little alley on your left. Turn down that little alley, and it will be the third gate on the right. . . ."
T1274	Quotation 205561 205595	"Chick! . . . Chick! . . . Chick!"
T1275	Quotation 205750 205769	"Whom do you want?"
T1276	Cue 205770 205775	asked
T1277	Entity 205776 205785	the woman
T1278	Quotation 205839 205854	"Good-morning!"
T1279	Entity 205855 205868	Ivan Ivanitch
T1280	Cue 205869 205876	shouted
T1281	Quotation 205922 205983	"Tell me, please, does Nastasya Petrovna Toskunov live here?"
T1282	Quotation 205984 206021	"Yes! But what do you want with her?"
T1283	Quotation 206022 206058	"Perhaps you are Nastasya Petrovna?"
T1284	Quotation 206059 206077	"Well, yes, I am!"
T1285	Quotation 206078 206348	"Very pleased to see you. . . . You see, your old friend Olga Ivanovna Knyasev sends her love to you. This is her little son. And I, perhaps you remember, am her brother Ivan Ivanitch. . . . You are one of us from N.. . . You were born among us and married there. . . ."
T1286	Quotation 206593 206609	"Olga Ivanovna!"
T1287	Entity 206610 206613	she
T1288	Cue 206614 206622	screamed
T1289	Quotation 206652 206752	"My own darling! Ah, holy saints, why am I standing here like a fool? My pretty little angel. . . ."
T1290	Quotation 206837 206847	"Heavens!"
T1291	Entity 206848 206851	she
T1292	Cue 206852 206856	said
T1293	Quotation 206878 207018	"Olga's little boy! How delightful! He is his mother all over! The image of his mother! But why are you standing in the yard? Come indoors."
T1294	Quotation 207134 207167	"The room has not been done yet,"
T1295	Entity 207168 207171	she
T1296	Cue 207172 207176	said
T1297	Quotation 207279 207428	"Oh, Mother of God! Vassilisa, go and open the shutters anyway! My little angel! My little beauty! I did not know that Olitchka had a boy like that!"
T1298	Cue 207939 207944	asked
T1299	Entity 207896 207906	Yegorushka
T1300	Quotation 207946 207965	"What's your name?"
T1301	Entity 207966 207981	The little girl
T1302	Entity 207917 207920	her
T1303	Quotation 208055 208068	"Atka. . . ."
T1304	Cue 208038 208046	answered
T1305	Quotation 208087 208111	"He will live with you,"
T1306	Entity 208112 208125	Ivan Ivanitch
T1307	Quotation 208162 208280	"if you will be so kind, and we will pay ten roubles a month for his keep. He is not a spoilt boy; he is quiet. . . ."
T1308	Quotation 208281 208330	"I really don't know what to say, Ivan Ivanitch!"
T1309	Entity 208331 208348	Nastasya Petrovna
T1310	Quotation 208367 208497	"Ten roubles a month is very good, but it is a dreadful thing to take another person's child! He may fall ill or something. . . ."
T1311	Entity 208552 208565	Ivan Ivanitch
T1312	Entity 208503 208513	Yegorushka
T1313	Quotation 208623 208663	"Well, let him stay with you now, then,"
T1314	Cue 208606 208612	saying
T1315	Quotation 208613 208621	good-bye
T1316	Entity 208664 208666	he
T1317	Cue 208667 208671	said
